# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  TapAway — monorepo environment overview
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each app has its OWN .env file. Copy the examples inside each:
#
#   cp backend/.env.example  backend/.env
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#
# ── backend/.env  (the Express API → Railway) ────────────────
#   DATABASE_URL   PostgreSQL connection string (Railway Postgres)
#   AUTH_SECRET    Secret for signing JWTs  →  openssl rand -base64 32
#   PORT           API port (Railway sets this; local defaults to 4000)
#   CORS_ORIGIN    Allowed browser origin(s), e.g. http://localhost:3000
#
# ── frontend/.env  (the Next.js app → Vercel) ────────────────
#   BACKEND_API_URL       URL of the backend API (http://localhost:4000 in dev)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  Public site URL (http://localhost:3000 in dev)
#
# Only the backend touches the database and signs tokens. The frontend
# proxies API calls server-side, so no secret lives in the frontend.
